---
// src/pages/drinksisip.astro
// Case study for drinksisip.com, a living list of hot chocolates in New York.
// A short read: why it exists, then how it was built. Adapted from the
// Substack post "Designing Drinks I Sip".
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const links = [
  { label: 'drinksisip.com', title: 'Visit the site', href: 'https://drinksisip.com' },
  { label: 'Substack', title: 'Designing Drinks I Sip', href: 'https://avyaykashyap.substack.com/p/designing-drinks-i-sip-build-tools' },
];

const lessons = [
  {
    title: 'Every decision saved time.',
    body: 'The sandbox, the configurator and its knobs were all ways to spend less of my evenings on the parts that did not need me.',
  },
  {
    title: 'When words get hard, change the medium.',
    body: 'The moment describing a change became difficult, a knob or a slider did the job better than another prompt.',
  },
];
---

<Layout title="Drinks I Sip — Avyay" links={links}>
  <article class="case-study dk" data-chapters="Drinks I Sip">

    <header class="dk-hero">
      <span class="type-body-sm text-disabled">/Side project</span>
      <h1 class="type-title">Drinks I Sip</h1>
      <p class="dk-prose type-body-md">A living list of the hot chocolates I've had in New York and Jersey City. Every place gets a score, a pin on the map and a cup of its own. <a href="https://drinksisip.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit drinksisip.com</a>.</p>
      <figure class="dk-media" data-cover="drinksisip">
        <video class="clip" src="/assets/drinksisip/drinksisip-site.mp4" poster="/assets/drinksisip/drinksisip-site-poster.jpg" preload="none" muted loop playsinline aria-label="Screen recording of drinksisip.com: picking a place from the list flips the split-flap header to its name, flies the map to it and swaps in its cup"></video>
      </figure>
    </header>

    <section class="dk-meta">
      <div class="dk-meta-item"><span class="type-h4">Role</span><span class="type-body-sm">Design & build</span></div>
      <div class="dk-meta-item"><span class="type-h4">Built with</span><span class="type-body-sm">Claude Code, Paper</span></div>
      <div class="dk-meta-item"><span class="type-h4">Stack</span><span class="type-body-sm">MapLibre, three.js</span></div>
      <div class="dk-meta-item"><span class="type-h4">Timeline</span><span class="type-body-sm">Aug - Oct 2026</span></div>
    </section>

    <section id="why" class="dk-section" data-chapter="Why">
      <h2 class="dk-label type-h4">Why I built it</h2>
      <h3 class="dk-statement type-h1">A spreadsheet is a clumsy way to recommend a drink.</h3>
      <p class="dk-prose type-body-md">Seasonal drinks are my favourite, and hot chocolate is the most permanent of them. Inspired by Rachel Brotman's list, I started ranking my own, with a rubric that leans toward the dark, rich cups I like.</p>
      <p class="dk-prose type-body-md">Friends and colleagues kept asking where to go. Sending them a spreadsheet full of my methodology changes and metadata felt like the wrong answer, so I built a site anyone could open: the list, where each place is, and what the cup looks like.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="cups" class="dk-section" data-chapter="The cups">
      <h2 class="dk-label type-h4">How: the cups</h2>
      <h3 class="dk-statement type-h1">One paper cup for everyone was unmemorable.</h3>
      <p class="dk-prose type-body-md">The first idea was a single 3D paper cup with a 2D sleeve. But places like Max Brenner and MarieBelle serve in beautiful cups, and a generic one erased that. Prompting each cup or modelling them in Blender would have taken forever, so I asked Claude to build a three.js sandbox, starting with five vessels.</p>

      <div class="dk-pair">
        <figure class="dk-media">
          <video class="clip" src="/assets/drinksisip/vessels-sandbox.mp4" poster="/assets/drinksisip/vessels-sandbox-poster.jpg" preload="none" muted loop playsinline aria-label="Screen recording of the vessels sandbox: a goblet, mug, bell glass, tumbler and paper cup with marshmallows, switching between shapes and spinning"></video>
        </figure>
        <figure class="dk-media">
          <img src="/assets/drinksisip/vessels-wireframe.jpg" alt="The same five vessels in wireframe, showing each lathe profile and the heart-shaped marshmallows" width="2000" height="1140" loading="lazy" />
        </figure>
      </div>

      <p class="dk-prose type-body-md">The sandbox grew into a configurator: glass, finish, label style, marshmallows, size, tilt and chocolate colour, saved per place. For tiny adjustments I asked for knobs, because describing them in words would have burned through my token limit. Configurations save as JSON that I upload by hand, which keeps the <a href="https://drinksisip.com/vessels.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">configurator</a> public with no login.</p>

      <figure class="dk-media">
        <video class="clip" src="/assets/drinksisip/cup-configurator.mp4" poster="/assets/drinksisip/cup-configurator-poster.jpg" preload="none" muted loop playsinline aria-label="Screen recording of the cup configurator: choosing a place, then changing the glass, finish, label and marshmallows with buttons and sliders"></video>
      </figure>

      <p class="dk-prose type-body-md">The labels I drew in Paper. Since most places pour into plain white paper cups, I put each logo on the cup rather than copying their packaging.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="hold" class="dk-section" data-chapter="Holding the cup">
      <h2 class="dk-label type-h4">How: holding the cup</h2>
      <div class="dk-two">
        <figure class="dk-media">
          <video class="clip" src="/assets/drinksisip/hold-cup.mp4" poster="/assets/drinksisip/hold-cup-poster.jpg" preload="none" muted loop playsinline aria-label="Screen recording on a phone: scrolling through places swaps the cup, then Hold cup turns on the camera and the No Chewing Allowed cup appears in a hand and follows it"></video>
        </figure>
        <div>
          <h3 class="dk-statement type-h1">Then I wanted to hold it.</h3>
          <p class="dk-prose type-body-md">A cup on a screen is still a picture. On a phone, Hold cup turns on the camera and uses handPose to track your fingers, so the cup sits in your grip and moves with your hand.</p>
          <p class="dk-prose type-body-md">It's the closest the site gets to handing you the drink before you go and get it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="lessons" class="dk-section" data-chapter="What I learnt">
      <h2 class="dk-label type-h4">What I learnt</h2>
      <ol class="dk-lessons">
        {lessons.map(({ title, body }) => (
          <li class="dk-lesson">
            <h3 class="type-h3">{title}</h3>
            <p class="dk-body type-body-sm">{body}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <a class="dk-card" href="https://avyaykashyap.substack.com/p/designing-drinks-i-sip-build-tools" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <span class="type-h4">Substack</span>
        <span class="dk-card-title type-h2">Designing Drinks I Sip: Build tools that help you make decisions</span>
        <span class="dk-body type-body-sm">The longer version: the research agents, the geocoding skill, the cups and the labels.</span>
        <span class="dk-card-link type-body-sm"><span class="dk-diamond" aria-hidden="true"></span>Read the post ↗</span>
      </a>
    </section>

  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .dk {
    max-width: 860px;
    padding: 80px clamp(24px, 8vw, 100px) 120px;
  }

  .dk-prose {
    max-width: 680px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .dk-prose + .dk-prose {
    margin-top: 12px;
  }

  .dk-prose a {
    color: var(--color-text-accent);
  }

  .dk-hero {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  /* Recordings and screenshots sit on a soft panel, like the homepage covers */
  .dk-media {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 12px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--color-cool-bg);
  }

  .dk-media video,
  .dk-media img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }

  .dk-hero .dk-media {
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  .dk-section .dk-media,
  .dk-pair {
    margin: 32px 0;
  }

  .dk-pair {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .dk-pair .dk-media {
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* A portrait phone recording beside its text */
  .dk-two {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 260px 1fr;
    gap: 40px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .dk-meta {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 24px 32px;
  }

  .dk-meta-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }

  .dk-meta-item .type-body-sm {
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--color-text-strong);
  }

  .dk-section {
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding-top: 48px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .dk-label {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .dk-statement {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .dk-lessons {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 32px;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    counter-reset: lesson;
  }

  .dk-lesson {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    counter-increment: lesson;
  }

  .dk-lesson::before {
    content: counter(lesson, decimal-leading-zero);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-text-accent);
  }

  .dk-body {
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  /* The link out to the Substack post, with the homepage's "View work." hover */
  .dk-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding: 24px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--color-cool-bg);
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .dk-card:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent-outline);
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .dk-card-title {
    max-width: 560px;
    color: var(--color-text-strong);
  }

  .dk-card-link {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    margin-top: 8px;
    color: var(--color-text-strong);
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .dk-diamond {
    width: 4px;
    height: 4px;
    background: currentColor;
    transform: rotate(45deg);
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  .dk-card:hover .dk-card-link {
    color: var(--color-text-accent);
  }

  .dk-card:hover .dk-diamond {
    transform: rotate(90deg);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .dk {
      padding-top: 48px;
    }

    .dk-meta {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }

    .dk-pair,
    .dk-two,
    .dk-lessons {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .dk-two .dk-media {
      max-width: 280px;
    }
  }
</style>
